From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:02:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] editor field engine: natural terrain noise and mixing ops for
 the Fields panel's Generate section (rotate option for noise octaves,
 fractal, amplitude, terrain_mix, keep_side)

Plain fractal noise put every octave on the same lattice (all octaves are exactly 0 at the coarse lattice points: a visible grid of dimples, straight seams in ridged / billow) and
used 8 gradient directions (4 on the axes). `rotate = 1` (perlin, simplex, ridged, billow, musgrave, fbm_damped; default 0 keeps every old result and golden bit identical) puts every
octave in its own frame (golden angle turn and shift) with 64 gradient directions.

New ops in EdFieldLand.cpp: fractal (fbm / billow / ridged multifractal, domain warp limited to a quarter wavelength per octave, slope dependent detail, finest wavelength, soft limited
0..1 output), amplitude (zero-mean relief with an exact size), terrain_mix (add / multiply / raise only / lower only / replace with strength and mask), keep_side (water level clamp).
Tests: tests/EdLandTest.cpp (determinism at 1..8 threads, world position only, exact amplitude, blend / mask / water maths, lattice and isotropy checks), registered in
scripts/ed_native_tests.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F37er45a7etRuMgEW1q3kY

